{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"6ac7903b6e0c","type":"group","x":1430,"y":1740,"width":1320,"height":2490,"color":"5","label":"UEFI + GPT"},
		{"id":"4923c07eac04","type":"group","x":330,"y":5740,"width":1600,"height":1030,"color":"4","label":"Direct comparison: BIOS + MBR vs UEFI + GPT"},
		{"id":"1c301cbc6b0f","type":"group","x":-30,"y":1750,"width":860,"height":1780,"color":"2","label":"Legacy BIOS + MBR"},
		{"id":"da87e9375b40","type":"group","x":930,"y":2020,"width":400,"height":2210,"color":"3","label":"Key idea"},
		{"id":"971b35455633","type":"group","x":-30,"y":8570,"width":1780,"height":430,"color":"3","label":"Practice lab"},
		{"id":"c409dc83f23f","type":"group","x":330,"y":6870,"width":1600,"height":470,"color":"1","label":"Attack surface by boot stage"},
		{"id":"6c280f90f165","type":"group","x":-30,"y":7770,"width":2000,"height":350,"color":"1","label":"Example: UEFI bootkit"},
		{"id":"879994cb0f64","type":"group","x":-30,"y":9100,"width":2060,"height":310,"color":"4","label":"Study next and official references"},
		{"id":"1ef38bfee6e3","type":"group","x":-30,"y":0,"width":1960,"height":310,"color":"6","label":"Overview"},
		{"id":"67145fc89204","type":"group","x":-30,"y":7440,"width":2400,"height":230,"color":"1","label":"Example: MBR bootkit"},
		{"id":"3dd1c858e5ab","type":"group","x":930,"y":4330,"width":400,"height":1310,"color":"6","label":"Both paths converge: the Windows boot"},
		{"id":"8b941f503a03","type":"group","x":-30,"y":8220,"width":2000,"height":250,"color":"4","label":"Verify your boot architecture"},
		{"id":"103e639436b7","type":"group","x":930,"y":410,"width":400,"height":1230,"color":"6","label":"Common start: hardware initialization"},
		{"id":"72b831a258a5","type":"text","text":"**0x1BE to 0x1EE · 4 × 16 bytes**\nPartition entries: type, starting LBA, sector count, active flag","x":0,"y":2370,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"794303e0013b","type":"text","text":"**3 · Run MBR bootstrap code**\nThe CPU executes the boot code loaded from the MBR","x":460,"y":2370,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"6dc1b02f0dae","type":"text","text":"**0x1FE · 2 bytes**\nBoot signature `55 AA` marks a valid MBR boot sector","x":0,"y":2670,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"acb3b20354cd","type":"text","text":"**4 · Find the active partition**\nScans the partition table for the active primary partition (flag `0x80`)","x":460,"y":2660,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c9c8501edb47","type":"text","text":"**Windows Boot Manager**\n`bootmgr` (BIOS) or `bootmgfw.efi` (UEFI) reads the BCD store, normally `\\EFI\\Microsoft\\Boot\\BCD` on UEFI systems","x":960,"y":4390,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"58cfd33a14b1","type":"text","text":"**Windows OS Loader**\n`winload.exe` (BIOS) or `winload.efi` (UEFI) loads `ntoskrnl.exe`, the HAL and boot-start drivers","x":960,"y":4690,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"64f6e4372a66","type":"text","text":"**ExitBootServices (UEFI only)**\nWindows takes over the machine from the firmware boot environment","x":960,"y":4950,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c0ae60ae612e","type":"text","text":"**Kernel initialization**\n`ntoskrnl.exe` sets up memory management, drivers, processes and system services","x":960,"y":5190,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"08acea6ead15","type":"text","text":"**Windows starts**\n`smss.exe` (Session Manager) and other user-mode components initialize, then logon","x":960,"y":5450,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8291109c8905","type":"text","text":"## MBR structure\nFirst 512-byte logical sector (LBA 0) of the boot disk","x":0,"y":1810,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"13169bc2fce8","type":"text","text":"**1 · BIOS firmware**\nPOST, device init, selects the boot disk","x":460,"y":1810,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a185fe7dcb9f","type":"text","text":"**2 · Read MBR (LBA 0)**\nLoads the first 512-byte sector into memory, traditionally at `0x7C00`","x":460,"y":2080,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"4987d33a52ca","type":"text","text":"**Key difference**\nNot simply MBR vs GPT. It is how the firmware finds and executes the bootloader.","x":960,"y":2080,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"aad407935b30","type":"text","text":"**BIOS + MBR**\n# Code → Code → Code\nFirmware loads disk code, which finds another boot sector, which loads the Windows boot manager.","x":960,"y":2640,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c7b2db7f3bac","type":"text","text":"**Disk layout**\nLBA 0: MBR · Partition 1: VBR + `bootmgr` (system partition) · Partition 2: Windows C: with `winload.exe`, `ntoskrnl.exe`","x":0,"y":2960,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6be06f5a1e56","type":"text","text":"**UEFI + GPT**\n# Entry → File → Loader\nFirmware follows a boot entry, finds an EFI executable and launches the Windows boot manager.","x":960,"y":3290,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"de59678aef2e","type":"text","text":"**Why it matters**\nUEFI loads `bootmgfw.efi` from the ESP without executing code from LBA 0 or the partition's first sector.","x":960,"y":4000,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"950f9a88d074","type":"text","text":"**1 · Power ON**\nPower supply feeds the motherboard and CPU","x":960,"y":470,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5c502a0794da","type":"text","text":"**2 · CPU initialization**\nCPU starts executing firmware instructions from its reset vector","x":960,"y":710,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"105f08c73a82","type":"text","text":"**3 · Firmware execution**\nBIOS or UEFI firmware runs its initialization code","x":960,"y":950,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"4a3e7145097a","type":"text","text":"**4 · POST**\nFirmware initializes and checks hardware: RAM, CPU, chipset, storage","x":960,"y":1190,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c8a2bd3395fb","type":"text","text":"**5 · Boot device selection**\nFirmware picks a boot device from its boot configuration. The two architectures diverge here.","x":960,"y":1450,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0d6dad493c59","type":"text","text":"**0x000 · 446 bytes**\nBootstrap code and disk metadata","x":0,"y":2100,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"69f56ba58311","type":"text","text":"**5 · Load the VBR**\nLoads the first sector of the selected partition (Volume Boot Record)","x":460,"y":2980,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1c3a2dce0944","type":"text","text":"**Clarification**\nBIOS understands neither NTFS nor GPT, and the MBR code does not parse NTFS. It only finds the partition boot sector. System and Windows partitions can be different.","x":0,"y":3280,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"86cdea4774b3","type":"text","text":"**6 · Windows partition boot code**\nLoads the next Windows boot component, traditionally `bootmgr`","x":460,"y":3310,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1618d533da44","type":"text","text":"# Disk Boot Process\nMBR vs GPT: from power-on to the Windows kernel","x":0,"y":100,"width":360,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e073c449f640","type":"text","text":"**Scope**\nFollows the whole boot chain from pressing the power button until Windows starts running applications. Two architectures: legacy BIOS + MBR and UEFI + GPT.","x":460,"y":70,"width":400,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"35de13d4c2d2","type":"text","text":"**Terminology**\nGPT and MBR are partitioning schemes. UEFI and BIOS are firmware interfaces. The pairings are conventional; exceptions and compatibility mechanisms exist.","x":960,"y":60,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a29da08670b6","type":"text","text":"**Legend**\nPurple = common steps · Orange = BIOS + MBR · Cyan = UEFI + GPT · Green = on-disk structures · Yellow = notes · Red = attacks and warnings","x":1460,"y":70,"width":440,"height":200},
		{"id":"1dfd31f12e22","type":"text","text":"## GPT disk layout\nTypical 512-byte-sector disk","x":1920,"y":1820,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c590d8b39af9","type":"text","text":"**5 · Data D: (276.74 GB)**\nNTFS: personal files and games","x":2380,"y":3330,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"02735c36b3d1","type":"text","text":"**7 · Read FAT32**\nThe firmware's own filesystem support reads the EFI executable","x":1460,"y":3680,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b9659e269139","type":"text","text":"**Notes**\nSEC, PEI, DXE and BDS are common UEFI PI phases; platforms differ. Secure Boot is optional. Firmware follows its boot entry; it does not search the disk for `bootmgfw.efi`.","x":1920,"y":3620,"width":340,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ad08a3b2ab9b","type":"text","text":"**8 · Load `bootmgfw.efi`**\nWindows Boot Manager loads as a UEFI PE/COFF executable. With Secure Boot on, firmware validates its signature.","x":1460,"y":4000,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"719a7de5d19a","type":"text","text":"## Example GPT disk\n476.92 GB SSD. Logical view, not byte-accurate","x":2380,"y":1810,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"6f47407f072d","type":"text","text":"**LBA 0 · Protective MBR**\nType `0xEE` entry marks the disk as GPT; kept for old partitioning tools","x":1920,"y":2080,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"507c30377f1d","type":"text","text":"**1 · EFI System Partition (100 MB)**\nFAT32: `EFI/Microsoft/Boot/` with `bootmgfw.efi` and `BCD`","x":2380,"y":2080,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0c4efd1b836e","type":"text","text":"**3 · DXE phase**\nFirmware drivers and services load; storage controllers become available","x":1460,"y":2360,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"e7801caeb05a","type":"text","text":"**LBA 1 · Primary GPT header**\nSignature `EFI PART`, CRC32, disk GUID, partition array location","x":1920,"y":2370,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"56f90daddf37","type":"text","text":"**4 · BDS phase**\nBoot Device Selection: firmware processes its boot configuration","x":1460,"y":2670,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"043dabdb4b4c","type":"text","text":"**LBA 2 to 33 · Partition entry array**\nThe actual GPT partition table entries","x":1920,"y":2660,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4c8730554a02","type":"text","text":"**3 · Windows C: (199.23 GB)**\nNTFS: `Windows/System32/` with `winload.efi` and `ntoskrnl.exe`","x":2380,"y":2670,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"05545dde9df2","type":"text","text":"**5 · Read NVRAM boot entries**\nChecks `BootOrder` and the matching `Boot####` variables","x":1460,"y":2990,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f784b7db8acb","type":"text","text":"**LBA 34 onward**\nUsable disk space and partitions","x":1920,"y":3000,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5593ab6a4aa9","type":"text","text":"**1 · SEC phase**\nSecurity and initial processor state; temporary memory may be set up","x":1460,"y":1800,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"9188a754952b","type":"text","text":"**2 · PEI phase**\nEarly hardware initialization, including memory","x":1460,"y":2090,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4003918f2419","type":"text","text":"**2 · MSR (16 MB)**\nMicrosoft Reserved, no file system","x":2380,"y":2370,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2f4916e7e201","type":"text","text":"**4 · Recovery (870 MB)**\nWindows Recovery Environment","x":2380,"y":3000,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"45c5fd3a36f6","type":"text","text":"**6 · Locate the ESP**\nUses the entry's device path and GPT partition info to find the EFI System Partition","x":1460,"y":3310,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4eb74691dd55","type":"text","text":"**Near end of disk**\nBackup partition entry array, then the backup GPT header at the last LBA","x":1920,"y":3310,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c7ce92e36d68","type":"text","text":"**GPT metadata**\nPartition table tampering → disk structure manipulation","x":1160,"y":6930,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cb8298f18d51","type":"text","text":"**EFI System Partition**\nMalicious EFI executable → UEFI boot persistence","x":1560,"y":6930,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"692548bf130d","type":"text","text":"**Windows loader**\nLoader tampering → early OS compromise","x":1160,"y":7170,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"001cd81b508a","type":"text","text":"**Bootloader location**\nBIOS + MBR: Partition boot sector leads to `bootmgr`\nUEFI + GPT: EFI System Partition","x":760,"y":6040,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"ee4a86ae0fd1","type":"text","text":"**Windows loader**\nBIOS + MBR: `winload.exe`\nUEFI + GPT: `winload.efi`","x":760,"y":6300,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"74dde53cb702","type":"text","text":"**Kernel**\nBIOS + MBR: `ntoskrnl.exe`\nUEFI + GPT: `ntoskrnl.exe`","x":1160,"y":6300,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"285048b4563d","type":"text","text":"**Secure Boot**\nBIOS + MBR: Not part of legacy BIOS\nUEFI + GPT: Supported","x":360,"y":6560,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"76d99a465c07","type":"text","text":"**BIOS/UEFI firmware**\nFirmware implant → firmware persistence","x":360,"y":6930,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b503c493a9b8","type":"text","text":"**MBR**\nMBR bootkit → pre-OS persistence","x":760,"y":6940,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"abe80d9241d2","type":"text","text":"**Windows Boot Manager**\nBootloader modification → boot-chain compromise","x":360,"y":7170,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"9db4bfa271fc","type":"text","text":"**BCD**\nBoot configuration manipulation → changed boot behavior","x":760,"y":7170,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"394dc88efa70","type":"text","text":"**Kernel**\nKernel-level rootkit → privileged persistence","x":1560,"y":7170,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"88a62294f7d8","type":"text","text":"**Firmware**\nBIOS + MBR: Legacy BIOS\nUEFI + GPT: UEFI","x":360,"y":5800,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"831e71ac8e52","type":"text","text":"**Partition metadata**\nBIOS + MBR: LBA 0\nUEFI + GPT: LBA 1 and entry array","x":760,"y":5800,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"db0f0c6af1e5","type":"text","text":"**Initial boot target**\nBIOS + MBR: MBR bootstrap code\nUEFI + GPT: Firmware boot entry","x":1160,"y":5800,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"d51d9ce6ded5","type":"text","text":"**Executes MBR code?**\nBIOS + MBR: Yes\nUEFI + GPT: No","x":1560,"y":5800,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"c8448d1ad1e2","type":"text","text":"**Finds bootloader through**\nBIOS + MBR: Active partition\nUEFI + GPT: NVRAM device path","x":360,"y":6050,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"4d6be38ac6e8","type":"text","text":"**Bootloader format**\nBIOS + MBR: Boot code / Windows boot manager\nUEFI + GPT: `.efi` executable","x":1160,"y":6040,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"3c39f64d7518","type":"text","text":"**System partition FS**\nBIOS + MBR: Usually NTFS\nUEFI + GPT: FAT32 ESP","x":1560,"y":6050,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"3ca079360560","type":"text","text":"**Boot configuration**\nBIOS + MBR: BCD\nUEFI + GPT: BCD","x":360,"y":6300,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"95ee273cb037","type":"text","text":"**Backup partition metadata**\nBIOS + MBR: No standard backup\nUEFI + GPT: Yes","x":1560,"y":6300,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"cde8fa6b96a7","type":"text","text":"**Windows boot options**\nWindows can boot via UEFI from GPT or legacy BIOS from MBR. Standard Windows UEFI installs require GPT for the boot disk.","x":760,"y":6540,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5b6236d322c0","type":"text","text":"## Practice lab\n**Use VMs.** Don't modify your real laptop's boot sectors.","x":0,"y":8730,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"64880bd95f49","type":"text","text":"**Investigation tasks**\n- Inspect LBA 0 on both disks (HxD or a forensic hex viewer)\n- Identify the MBR signature `55 AA`\n- Find the GPT signature `EFI PART`\n- Inspect the GPT partition entries\n- Locate the ESP and examine `bootmgfw.efi`\n- Compare BCD locations in BIOS vs UEFI installs\n- Break the boot config in a disposable VM and observe","x":1200,"y":8630,"width":520,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9c7933b15e55","type":"text","text":"## Study next\nThe UEFI boot chain: `BootOrder`, `Boot####`, EFI executables, BCD and Secure Boot. It connects to bootkit detection, firmware security and Windows incident response.","x":0,"y":9160,"width":380,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5469a0c646c7","type":"text","text":"[UEFI Specification: GPT Disk Layout](https://uefi.org/specs/UEFI/2.10/05_GUID_Partition_Table_Format.html)\n_official reference_","x":460,"y":9200,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"d0f835ecd32f","type":"text","text":"[UEFI Specification: Boot Manager](https://uefi.org/specs/UEFI/2.10/03_Boot_Manager.html)\n_official reference_","x":860,"y":9210,"width":340,"height":120},
		{"id":"434c5465570d","type":"text","text":"[Microsoft: UEFI/GPT-based Windows partitions](https://learn.microsoft.com/windows-hardware/manufacture/desktop/configure-uefigpt-based-hard-drive-partitions?view=windows-11)\n_official reference_","x":1260,"y":9200,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"191c2546a767","type":"text","text":"[Microsoft: Windows boot process and troubleshooting](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ie/troubleshoot/windows-client/performance/windows-boot-issues-troubleshooting)\n_official reference_","x":1660,"y":9200,"width":340,"height":140},
		{"id":"8d36fa855c84","type":"text","text":"```\nEFI/\n ├─ Microsoft/Boot/\n │   └─ bootmgfw.efi\n └─ Malicious/\n     └─ payload.efi\n```","x":400,"y":7830,"width":340,"height":260},
		{"id":"4dc8f72a6cee","type":"text","text":"## Verify your own boot setup\nRun in PowerShell, don't assume","x":0,"y":8300,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"eef05990d030","type":"text","text":"**A · Firmware type**\n`(Get-ComputerInfo).BiosFirmwareType`\nExpect `Uefi`","x":400,"y":8280,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"f2d4db3a39c9","type":"text","text":"**B · Secure Boot**\n`Confirm-SecureBootUEFI`\nExpect `True` (`False` if disabled)","x":800,"y":8280,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"9c2664949e6a","type":"text","text":"**C · Boot Manager**\n`bcdedit /enum \"{bootmgr}\"`\nLook for path `\\EFI\\Microsoft\\Boot\\bootmgfw.efi`","x":1200,"y":8280,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"6b20c0f57fda","type":"text","text":"**D · Firmware entries**\n`bcdedit /enum firmware`\nBoot configuration exposed through Windows","x":1600,"y":8280,"width":340,"height":160},
		{"id":"7b1aa8de3438","type":"text","text":"**Lab A · BIOS + MBR**\nVM with legacy BIOS firmware and an MBR-partitioned virtual disk","x":400,"y":8730,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"58e50b8cef18","type":"text","text":"**Lab B · UEFI + GPT**\nVM with UEFI firmware and a GPT-partitioned virtual disk","x":800,"y":8730,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b74308f2ed7a","type":"text","text":"## Example: MBR bootkit\nAttacker with enough privileges modifies the MBR bootstrap code","x":0,"y":7500,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b04ab7201c48","type":"text","text":"**1 · Modified MBR runs**\nBIOS executes the altered bootstrap code","x":400,"y":7500,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ba0b80ba27eb","type":"text","text":"**2 · Runs before Windows**\nMalicious code executes pre-OS","x":800,"y":7510,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"979ef94ad8ad","type":"text","text":"**3 · Loads more code**\nIt may pull in additional malicious code","x":1200,"y":7500,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2d53195157ff","type":"text","text":"**4 · Hands over control**\nTransfers to the legitimate boot process","x":1600,"y":7500,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"4e4c7f3de479","type":"text","text":"## Example: UEFI bootkit\nAttacker places a malicious EFI executable in the ESP","x":0,"y":7890,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"069894887923","type":"text","text":"**Not automatic**\nA `.efi` file sitting in the ESP does not run by itself.","x":800,"y":7890,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"853395007d6b","type":"text","text":"**Needs a valid boot path**\nA manipulated firmware boot entry or a compromised bootloader must reach it.","x":1200,"y":7880,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"5a511beca5ee","type":"text","text":"**Defense: Secure Boot**\nBlocks unauthorized EFI images, if its trust configuration and enforcement stay intact.","x":1600,"y":7880,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b3287ae591f8","type":"text","text":"**5 · Windows starts**\nThe user may notice nothing unusual","x":2000,"y":7500,"width":340,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{
			"id":"5241efdc5e22b790",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"#Forensics #Disk-FOR #boot-process ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":820,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"1e4d16b27130","fromNode":"1618d533da44","fromSide":"right","toNode":"e073c449f640","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"149260dd8f09","fromNode":"e073c449f640","fromSide":"right","toNode":"35de13d4c2d2","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"305097010a07","fromNode":"35de13d4c2d2","fromSide":"right","toNode":"a29da08670b6","toSide":"left"},
		{"id":"501a8346a994","fromNode":"950f9a88d074","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"5c502a0794da","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"120b81080eb4","fromNode":"5c502a0794da","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"105f08c73a82","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"90bbdb992dd2","fromNode":"105f08c73a82","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"4a3e7145097a","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"07411c541ac2","fromNode":"4a3e7145097a","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"c8a2bd3395fb","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"fc73643e5728","fromNode":"35de13d4c2d2","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"950f9a88d074","toSide":"top","label":"begin"},
		{"id":"5eca74c3970a","fromNode":"c8a2bd3395fb","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"13169bc2fce8","toSide":"top","label":"legacy BIOS"},
